# What git should ignore in a Photo Scout working directory
#
# The rule of thumb: track anything you WROTE or decided, ignore anything a
# program can rebuild. That keeps the history small and readable.

# ---- the virtual environment -------------------------------------------
# The README creates it as .venv; venv/ is the other common name. Either way
# requirements.txt is what records the dependencies, and that IS tracked.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- generated output ---------------------------------------------------
# Thumbnails, previews, reports and the score database are all produced by a
# scoring run. Tens of thousands of files; none of it is your work.
_photo_scout/*

# ...with one deliberate exception inside that folder.
# tags.json is your tagging: hand-authored, not derived from anything, and
# not reproducible by re-running.
!_photo_scout/tags.json
#
# calibration.json is NOT excepted. It is written automatically at the end of
# a scoring run and describes one particular library, so it is worth nothing
# to anybody else and is regenerated in seconds.

# ---- databases ----------------------------------------------------------
# scores.sqlite3 is regenerated by a rescore.
# publish.sqlite3 is the Ghost upload ledger: losing it is not destructive,
# but it would re-upload every image on the next publish and leave the old
# copies orphaned in Ghost. Worth a manual backup; not worth binary churn in
# every commit.
*.sqlite3

# ---- downloads from a published gallery ---------------------------------
# "Save tags" on the Ghost page downloads this. It is one visitor's tagging,
# fed back in with --web-tags, not part of the project.
psc-web-tags.json

# ---- the optional link-preview Worker -----------------------------------
# wrangler.toml carries your own domain and route; wrangler.toml.example, which
# carries example.com, is what's tracked. .wrangler/ is its local state.
worker/wrangler.toml
.wrangler/

# ---- operating system clutter -------------------------------------------
*.tmp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
